{
  "id": "04668_hasamaru",
  "headword": "{挟|はさ}まる",
  "reading": "はさまる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be caught between; to be sandwiched",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "る",
    "stem": "{挟|はさ}ま"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be caught between; to be sandwiched",
      "explanation": "To become stuck or trapped between two things."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to be inserted; to be placed between",
      "explanation": "For something to be positioned between two objects."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "04668_hasamaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{歯|は}に{食|た}べ{物|もの}が{挟|はさ}まった。",
      "english": "Food got stuck between my teeth.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04668_hasamaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{指|ゆび}がドアに{挟|はさ}まって{痛|いた}い。",
      "english": "My finger got caught in the door and it hurts.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04668_hasamaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{石|いし}が{靴|くつ}の{中|なか}に{挟|はさ}まって{歩|ある}きにくい。",
      "english": "A stone got stuck in my shoe and it's hard to walk.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04668_hasamaru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{手紙|てがみ}が{挟|はさ}まっていた。",
      "english": "A letter was tucked in.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04668_hasamaru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{本|ほん}の{間|あいだ}に{古|ふる}い{写真|しゃしん}が{挟|はさ}まっていた。",
      "english": "An old photograph was tucked between the books.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04668_hasamaru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{棚|たな}と{壁|かべ}の{間|あいだ}にリモコンが{挟|はさ}まっていて、なかなか{取|と}れなかった。",
      "english": "The remote was stuck between the shelf and the wall, and I couldn't get it out easily.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{挟|はさ}まる is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pair: {挟|はさ}む (transitive - to pinch, insert)\n- Pattern: Xが〜に{挟|はさ}まる\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{挟|はさ}まっている describes the result state where something is currently stuck or placed between.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {歯|は}に{挟|はさ}まる (to get stuck in teeth)\n- ドアに{挟|はさ}まる (to get caught in a door)\n- {間|あいだ}に{挟|はさ}まる (to be caught/placed between)\n\nOften used to describe uncomfortable situations like getting fingers caught or food stuck in teeth.",
